{
  "slug": "fellowship",
  "name": "Fellowship",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A LotR-themed multi-agent system for solo product devs. Gandalf orchestrates nine companions across product, architecture, engineering, review, security, testing, design, devops, and docs — with persistent project memory and conservative tiered routing.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **12 skills**, **9 agents**, **18 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (12): `accessibility` (Use when auditing for accessibility violations, fixing WCAG issues, building accessible components, or running screen reader tests), `autoimprove` (Use when an agent file shows recurring failures in a feedback log, or when running a scheduled improvement…), `brainstorming` (Use before creating features, building components, or planning complex work), `codebase-map` (Use when entering an unfamiliar codebase, or when companions report missing structural context), `design-it-twice` (Generate multiple radically different module/API designs in parallel and compare them on depth, simplicity, and leverage), `investigate` (Use when diagnosing a bug, test failure, deploy issue, or any unexpected behavior), `learn` (Use when Frodo asks 'what do you remember?', when memory references feel stale, or on explicit /fellowship:learn invocation), `planning` (Use after brainstorming to turn a design spec into an implementation plan), and 4 more\n- **Agents** (9): `aragorn` (The Fellowship's Product Manager — dispatch to define scope, surface risk, and produce requirements before any building begins), `arwen` (The Fellowship's Senior Product Designer — dispatch for design systems, UX audits, accessibility, Figma work, and visual exploration…), `bilbo` (The Fellowship's Technical Writer — dispatch for README, changelog, inline documentation, API docs, and architecture overviews), `boromir` (The Fellowship's Security Engineer — dispatch for security audits on auth, payments, data mutations, and public APIs), `gimli` (The Fellowship's engineer — dispatch for any task that creates or modifies code), `legolas` (The Fellowship's code reviewer — dispatch after Gimli completes implementation; never fixes code), `merry` (The Fellowship's Technical Architect — dispatch to evaluate approaches, produce architecture decision records, and define interface contracts before…), `pippin` (The Fellowship's test engineer — dispatch to fill test gaps, write TDD contracts, build test infrastructure, or verify…), and 1 more\n- **Commands** (18): `accessibility` (Loads the accessibility skill — WCAG 2.2 audits, screen-reader testing, ARIA remediation, and accessible-component guidance), `aragorn` (Loads Aragorn's product-management craft as an in-session skill), `arwen` (Loads Arwen's design thinking as an in-session skill), `bilbo` (Loads Bilbo's documentation lens as an in-session skill), `boromir` (Loads Boromir's security review lens as an in-session skill), `brainstorming` (Loads the brainstorming skill for in-session ideation work), `gimli` (Loads Gimli's builder craft as an in-session skill), `investigate` (Loads the investigate skill — systematic root-cause methodology for bugs, test failures, and unexpected behavior), and 10 more\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install fellowship@claude-community` from `KarolusD/fellowship`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 12,
    "agent": 9,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 18
  },
